555</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7309050-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7309050</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8310072-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8310072</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9014994-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9014994</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9126813-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9126813</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1063097A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OMURA KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OMURA, KUNIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OMURA KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OMURA, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A space (S) is defined for accommodating an optical sensor between a sensing gear (11) being a drive transmission gear and a frame (2) supporting the same. A comblike object part (11c) to be sensed is integrally formed on the inner wall of the sensing gear (11). An optical sensor (15) is so disposed that the object part (11c) passes between a light-emitting part (15a) and a light-receiving part (15b) of the optical sensor (15). The optical sensor (15) is protected from disturbances such as disturbance light and paper powder by means of the sensing gear (11) and the frame (2), thereby providing a highly reliable small-sized sensing mechanism.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>D'après cette invention, un espace (S) prévu pour recevoir un capteur optique est ménagé entre un galet de détection (11), qui consiste en un galet de transmission et d'entraînement, et un cadre (2) qui supporte ledit galet. Une partie objet de type peigne (11c) devant être détectée fait partie intégrante de la paroi interne du galet de détection (11). Un capteur optique (15) est disposé de sorte que la partie objet (11c) passe entre une partie émettrice de lumière (15a) et une partie réceptrice de lumière (15b) du capteur optique (15). Le capteur optique (15) est protégé des perturbations, telle que de la lumière parasite ou de la poudre de papier, par le galet de détection (11) et par le cadre (2), ce qui permet d'obtenir un mécanisme de détection d'une grande fiabilité et de taille réduite.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>